ID: vr-21
Title: Jaw-following head cutoff and live visible-neck control
GitHub issue: https://github.com/Zanark/Verona/issues/20

Status: DONE
Milestone: Visually adjustable curved head/neck boundary without a horizontal chop.
Dependencies: vr-14, vr-20

Purpose:
Owner rejects the straight neck/hair cutoff and draws a jaw-following contour.
Replace Head and neck's flat plane with a reversible model-space curve and a
live visible-neck slider. Preserve Claire, other views, motion and Full bust.

Tasks:
[x] 21.1 Add shared bounded jaw-profile parameters and conservative reduced
    topology, retaining primitives whose interiors can cross a curved boundary.
[x] 21.2 Clip all skin/hair/edge/point/depth passes consistently before XYZ,
    retain original motion IDs and bound the latest adjustable topology cache.
[x] 21.3 Provide live Visible neck 0-6 cm, per-view choices and stable framing;
    no audio regeneration/seek, FaceMesh keeps its separate front-only extent.
[x] 21.4 Verify curve, endpoints, malformed input, buffer replacement, pixels,
    transparent overlay, rotation, playback and appropriate local performance.
[x] 21.5 Prepare verified source with guide/book/index/ledger and issue/Project
    tracking; keep Realistic parked and existing release tags unchanged.

Acceptance criteria:
Head and neck has a visibly curved jaw-following lower edge, not a straight
horizontal plane. Slider preview lets the owner choose jaw-only or more neck.
Full bust round-trips exactly. Hidden primitives and normal work are reduced.
No interior-crossing curved primitive is discarded solely on corner signs.
Choices restore per view; repeated adjustments retain only the latest five
crop index buffers, no per-frame rebuild or speech/model/storage change.
No device activation, asset download, sibling interaction or new release.

